# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b1), edited. howie_butterman's first conversation.

~ start
set howie_butterman_met
Narrator: He tips his cap with two fingers, grinning like a terrier that has already dug up the bone.
howie_butterman [smile]: Welcome to the Founder's Round, friends. Deputy Howie Butterman, here to keep the peace and point newcomers the right way.
* Ask about his work with the watch -> about_work
* Ask about the village and its faiths -> about_village
* Ask if there has been any trouble -> rumour
* [Insight DC 14] Watch how eagerly he studies your group -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ about_work
howie_butterman [smile]: Constable Squire handles the scowling and cell keys; I handle the friendly word on the cobbles. Folk tell old Howie what they would never say across a desk.
-> menu

~ about_village
howie_butterman [neutral]: Most of us hold to the Old Ways and the square's oak, though you will see sunflowers on lintels and songbird ribbons down the lane.
-> menu

~ rumour
howie_butterman [sly]: Things will stir now you arrived with Lord Phillip and Lady Adela. The old barrow path past the heather has had strange lights all week.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
set cult_clue_howie_butterman
Narrator: As he leans in, a dried hare's foot on a cord slips from his collar, his pulse jumping with hungry excitement.
howie_butterman [smile]: We have been waiting on proper travelers to walk in with the gentry. Mark my words, the woods are ready for a change of season.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
Narrator: He adjusts his collar with a brisk tug and offers an easy, practiced wink.
howie_butterman [smile]: Do not mind me staring, friends. New faces are rare as dry boots round here.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask about his work with the watch -> about_work
* Ask about the village and its faiths -> about_village
* Ask if there has been any trouble -> rumour
* [Insight DC 14] Watch how eagerly he studies your group -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END
